# React & Next.js Conventions

## Component Structure
- Use function declarations for page components, named exports for shared components
- Client components must include 'use client' directive at the top of the file
- Server components are the default in the app directory — only add 'use client' when needed (state, effects, event handlers, browser APIs)
- Co-locate component-specific types in the same file; shared types go in `types/index.ts`

## Naming
- Components: PascalCase (`RoomCard.tsx`, `FilterBar.tsx`)
- Utilities/hooks: camelCase (`useRoomFilters.ts`, `formatCurrency.ts`)
- Pages: `page.tsx` inside route directories following Next.js App Router conventions
- Test files: `ComponentName.test.tsx` co-located next to the component

## Styling
- Use Tailwind CSS utility classes exclusively — no CSS modules or styled-components
- Use the `clsx` utility for conditional classes
- Responsive breakpoints: mobile-first (`sm:`, `md:`, `lg:`)
- Brand colors via `brand-*` tokens defined in tailwind.config.ts
- Shared component classes (`.btn-primary`, `.container-page`) are in globals.css `@layer components`

## State Management
- Local state with `useState` for component-specific state
- URL search params for filter/sort state that should be shareable
- No global state library — prop drilling is acceptable for this app's scale

## Imports
- Use `@/` path alias for all imports from the project root
- Group imports: React/Next → third-party → project libs → components → types
